# Architecture Decision Records

We record meaningful decisions in [docs/adr](docs/adr). Read existing ADRs before proposing a conflicting change.

Write an ADR when the choice has real alternatives and lasting consequences: module boundaries, dependency direction, state, API/data ownership, auth, rendering, caching, error handling, persistence.

Do not write ADRs for names, boilerplate, or other reversible details.

An ADR is short: context, problem, options, decision, consequences. After a meaningful change, update the matching ADR or overview if the decision shifted.

Template and examples live in [MENTOR_CONTEXT.MD](MENTOR_CONTEXT.MD) (ADR practice) and the existing files under `docs/adr`.
